(STATISTICAL TECHNIQUES - EXAMINATION & STUDY GUIDE) Tj
0 -24 Td
(Q1. What are the normal equations for fitting a straight line using the principle of least squares?) Tj
0 -16 Td
(Ans: For fitting a straight line y = a + bx to n pairs of observations, the normal equations are:) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  Equation 1: sum(y) = n*a + b*sum(x)) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  Equation 2: sum(x*y) = a*sum(x) + b*sum(x^2)) Tj
0 -16 Td
(Solving these two equations simultaneously yields the parameter constants a and b.) Tj
0 -24 Td
(Q2. Define the principle of least squares in statistical curve fitting.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(Ans: The principle of least squares minimizes the sum of squared differences between observed and fitted values.) Tj
0 -24 Td
(Q3. What is the difference between correlation and regression analysis?) Tj
0 -16 Td
(Ans: Correlation measures the degree and direction of linear association, while regression predicts a response.) Tj
0 -24 Td
(Q4. Explain the method of moments in parameter estimation.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(Ans: The method of moments equates population moments to sample moments to estimate distribution parameters.) Tj
0 -24 Td
(Q5. State the assumptions of ordinary least squares (OLS) regression.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(Ans: OLS assumes linearity, independent observations, homoscedasticity, and normally distributed errors.) Tj
